“Highest common ancestor” is nonstandard. If it means the common ancestor closest to the root, then for two existing nodes in one rooted binary tree it is simply the root. The function should also verify membership:
```python
def contains(root, target):
    return bool(root) and (root is target or contains(root.left,target) or contains(root.right,target))

def highest_common_ancestor(root, a, b):
    return root if root and contains(root,a) and contains(root,b) else None
```
If “highest” was intended to mean deepest/lowest, that is the usual LCA problem and requires a different algorithm.

